  "id": "henan_zhuizi",
  "name": "Henan zhuizi (zhuiqin-accompanied ballad singing)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung narrative of Henan named for its accompanying instrument, the zhuizi or zhuiqin, a fretless bowed fiddle with a long board-like neck; centred on Kaifeng and Zhengzhou, it spread across northern China and is on the national intangible cultural heritage list. The singer beats time on a pair of wooden clappers (jianban) while the fiddler follows the voice line by line (the zhuihu card is the zhuiqin and the paiban card, set to its two-piece form, stands in for the two-slat jianban).",
  "recipe": "classic East Asian early-1950s henan zhuizi, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment. narrative vocal imitating speech like zhuihu, paiban. chinese traditional teahouse. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, broadcast loudness EQ. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
